       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and, in overdose, prolonged vasodilatory shock. Nothing in the details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify a dose that high.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose, which can be titrated up.\n- **Amlodipine 30 mg PO once daily**, if the dose is deliberate. In that case, please confirm it and give the rationale, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that.\n\nOnce you tell me which one, I'll enter it right away."
      }
